' ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════
' SUBNET: 192.168.10.x  (single subnet — MANET + on-board MC↔FCC)
' ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════

package "Subnet  192.168.10.0/24\n(single subnet — L2 bridge via MANET Air Units; GCS, all MCs and each drone's FCC share it)" as EXT_NET #E8F4E8 {

  package "Drone assembly — on-board Ethernet switch (baseboard fabric)" as INT_NET #FFF4E4 {

    rectangle "Jetson eth0\n192.168.10.11  (MC_ETH_IP)\nsingle address (HIF-002 / HIF-004)\nUDP:8888 XRCE-DDS Agent (ethernet fallback)\nUDP:14555 mission protocol → FCC\nUDP:14556 flow relay ← FCC\nUDP:14557 HIL_GPS → FCC" as JET_EXT #A8CCEE

    rectangle "Pixhawk 6X Ethernet\n192.168.10.31  (FCC_ETH_IP)\nsingle address (NuttX: one IPv4)\nUDP:8888 XRCE-DDS Client\nUDP:14555 mission protocol\nUDP:14556 flow relay (send)\nUDP:14557 HIL_GPS (recv)\nUDP:14550 Channel A (GCS, via mavlink-router)" as PX4_EXT #FFD4A8

    rectangle "On-board Ethernet Switch\n10/100/1000\n(baseboard fabric — single switch)" as INT_SW #D0D8E8

    rectangle "MANET Air Unit\n(on-drone, gateway)\n192.168.10.1\nRJ45 → wireless mesh" as AU_DUT #C8E0C8

    rectangle "Gimbal IP Camera\n192.168.10.200\n(HIF-007, shared switch)\nRTSP/H.265 :8554" as GIMCAM #EDE0F8
  }

  rectangle "GCS Laptop\n192.168.10.10\nQGroundControl\nSends MAVLink 2/UDP" as GCS #B8DCA8

  rectangle "MANET Air Unit (GCS)\n192.168.10.x (GCS-side AU)" as AU_GCS #C8E0C8

  rectangle "Peer Drone MC #2\n192.168.10.12\nDRONE_ID=2" as PEER2 #D8C0F0

  rectangle "Peer Drone MC #3\n192.168.10.13\nDRONE_ID=3" as PEER3 #D8C0F0

  rectangle "Peer AU #2\n(Drone 2 Air Unit)" as AU2 #C8E0C8

  rectangle "Peer AU #3\n(Drone 3 Air Unit)" as AU3 #C8E0C8
}

' ── Wired connections on drone assembly ──────────
JET_EXT <-[#208040,thickness=2]-> INT_SW : eth0\n(on-board trace)
PX4_EXT <-[#208040,thickness=2]-> INT_SW : 100BASE-T\n(on-board trace, HIF-002)
INT_SW  <-[#208040,thickness=2]-> AU_DUT : 1000BASE-T · Cat 5e · ≤ 3 m\nJ3 RJ45 (HIF-004)
GIMCAM  <-[#20A070,thickness=2]-> INT_SW : 1000BASE-TX · JST-GH→RJ45 ≤2m\nJ15 (HIF-007, shared switch)

note bottom of INT_NET
  HIF-002: MC↔FCC Ethernet runs over the same
  192.168.10.x switch — no separate subnet. PX4's
  NuttX stack gives the Pixhawk ONE IPv4 address.
  UDP:8888 only used when FCC_TRANSPORT=ethernet.
  Default DDS transport is HIF-001 (ttyTHS1 serial).
  UDP:14555 (mission protocol), :14556 (flow relay)
  and :14557 (HIL_GPS) are ALWAYS active,
  regardless of FCC_TRANSPORT — stock PX4 has no
  DDS-writable mission topic (ICD IR-007).
end note

' ── MANET wireless links ─────────────────────────
AU_DUT  <-[#408040,thickness=2,dashed]-> AU_GCS  : MANET mesh\n(wireless)
AU_DUT  <-[#408040,thickness=1,dashed]-> AU2      : MANET mesh
AU_DUT  <-[#408040,thickness=1,dashed]-> AU3      : MANET mesh

' ── GCS wired to its AU ──────────────────────────
GCS     <-[#208040]-> AU_GCS  : Ethernet

' ── Peer MCs to peer AUs ─────────────────────────
PEER2   <-[#208040]-> AU2
PEER3   <-[#208040]-> AU3

' ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════
' PORT MAP TABLE
' ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════

package "UDP Port Map  (on 192.168.10.x)" as PORTS #F4F8FF {
  rectangle "MC ↔ FCC  (HIF-002, on-board)\nFCC 192.168.10.31: :8888 uXRCE-DDS (fallback)\n:14555 mission · :14556 flow relay (FCC→MC)\n:14557 HIL_GPS (MC→FCC)\nNot routed by mavlink-router" as PMF #F5ECF5

  rectangle "GCS → FCC  (Channel A)\nDst: 192.168.10.31:14550\nStandard PX4 MAVLink autopilot channel\nMC does NOT inject on this channel" as PA #F4EAD4

  rectangle "GCS → MC  (Channel B recv)\nDst: 192.168.10.11:14551\nMC_CMD_* commands · MISSION_COUNT\nHEARTBEAT · COMMAND_LONG" as PB1 #D4E8D4

  rectangle "MC → GCS  (Channel B send)\nDst: 192.168.10.10:14552\nMC_STATUS (50100)  ≥2 Hz\nMC_DETECTION (50101)  event\nMC_HEALTH (50103)  ≥1 Hz\nCOMMAND_ACK · STATUSTEXT" as PB2 #D4E8D4

  rectangle "GCS ↔ MC  (Channel C — mission plan library)\nOrchestrator recv: 192.168.10.11:14571\nOrchestrator send: 192.168.10.10:14572\nLoopback to mission_orchestrator_node: 14580\nMAVFTP CRUD · MC_MISSION_PLAN_ACTIVATE/ACK\nDone — GCS-004/GCS-006, MC side" as PC #D4E0EC

  rectangle "Swarm Heartbeat  [DESIGN ONLY —\nswarm_coordinator_node not yet implemented]\nSrc/Dst: .11↔.12↔.13 :14900\n1 Hz SWARM_HEARTBEAT\n40-byte binary protocol" as PSH #E8E8E8;line.dashed

  rectangle "Swarm Coordination  [DESIGN ONLY —\nswarm_coordinator_node not yet implemented]\nSrc/Dst: .11↔.12↔.13 :14901\nISR_CANDIDATE · ISR_RESULT\nVORONOI_PROPOSAL · VORONOI_ACCEPT\nPEER_STATE" as PSC #E8E8E8;line.dashed

  rectangle "Zenoh DDS Bridge\nSrc/Dst: .11↔.12↔.13 :7447 (TCP)\nzenoh-bridge-dds · peer mode\nForwards no topics by default —\nno cross-host DDS topic exists yet" as PZBD #D4E0F0

  rectangle "Gimbal Camera Source Stream  [DESIGN ONLY —\nperception_front_node not yet implemented]\nMC (client) → .200:8554\nRTSP/H.265 · perception_front_node\n(IFD-006, HIF-007)" as PGIM #E8E8E8;line.dashed

  rectangle "GCS Video Downlink — Stream A  [DESIGN ONLY —\nvideo_mux_node not yet implemented]\nMC .11:8555 → GCS\nRTSP/H.265 + metadata · video_mux_node\nIndependent of Channel A/B  (IFD-007)" as PVID #E8E8E8;line.dashed

  rectangle "GCS Video Downlink — Stream B  [DESIGN ONLY —\nvideo_mux_node not yet implemented]\nMC .11:8556 → GCS\nRTSP/H.265 + metadata · video_mux_node\nNo track_id — perception_down_node has\nno tracker  (IFD-007 §8.1a, added 2026-07-22)" as PVIDB #E8E8E8;line.dashed
}

note bottom of PORTS
  mavlink-router v4 handles Channel A/B/C routing
  (three independent mavlink-routerd processes in
  one container, GCS-001/MAVR-001/GCS-006). It
  listens on :14551 and forwards to GCS :14552 for
  Channel B; :14571/:14572 for Channel C. Channel A
  traffic (port 14550) passes through the MANET
  transparently to the FCC — the MC does not
  inspect or modify it.
  ──────────────────────────────────────────
  DESIGN ONLY entries above (dashed): swarm_coord's
  swarm_coordinator_node/formation_controller_node
  and video_downlink's perception_front_node/
  video_mux_node are all still 15-line scaffolds
  (constructor + one log line, no networking/RTSP
  code) as of 2026-09-08 — these ports exist only in
  SDD-MC-001.md/ICD-MC-001.md's design, not in any
  running code yet.
end note

' ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════
' NETPLAN CONFIG NOTE
' ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════

note right of JET_EXT
  Jetson eth0 carries ONE IP address (Netplan):
    192.168.10.11 / 24  (MC_ETH_IP)
  GCS, peer MCs and this drone's own Pixhawk
  (192.168.10.31, FCC_ETH_IP) are all reached on
  this one subnet through the on-board switch.
  ─────────────────────────────────
  The gimbal camera (192.168.10.200) is just
  another host on the 192.168.10.0/24 segment,
  reached through the SAME eth0/switch — it is
  NOT a second Jetson interface (no eth1).
end note

legend right
  | Line | Description |
  | <#208040><b>───</b> | Wired Ethernet (1000BASE-T) |
  | <#20A070><b>───</b> | Gimbal camera (shared switch, HIF-007) |
  | <#408040><b>- - -</b> | MANET wireless (L2 bridge) |
  | Dashed gray card | Design-only port — no code implements it yet (scaffold node) |
endlegend

EXT_NET -down[hidden]-> PORTS

